@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="policy-shell">
    <p class="auth-eyebrow">STDMS</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: October 31, 2026</p>

    <p>
        STDMS (Student &amp; Teacher Data Management System) is a school records workspace
        operated by your school's administration. This page explains, in plain language,
        what information the system stores, why, and how it is protected. If anything
        here is unclear, contact your school administrator.
    </p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Staff accounts</strong> — the name, school email address, role
            (for example Administrator or Instructor), and a securely hashed password
            for each staff member who signs in. We never store passwords in plain text.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>School records</strong> — students (name, email, date of birth, department),
            instructors, courses, enrollments and grades, office assignments, and daily
            attendance records entered by authorized staff.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Basic technical logs</strong> — the server keeps short-lived diagnostic
            logs (such as requested pages and error details) so administrators can
            troubleshoot problems. These logs are not used for advertising or profiling.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the information is used</h2>
    <p>
        Records are used only to run the school's day-to-day administration: keeping class
        lists, recording attendance, and letting authorized staff find and update the
        information they are responsible for. Access is limited by role — an instructor,
        for example, can only work with the courses assigned to them. We do not sell
        personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        STDMS uses a single essential cookie to keep you signed in. It contains no
        personal details beyond your sign-in session, it is never used for advertising
        or cross-site tracking, and it is sent only over the encrypted (HTTPS) connection.
        The site does not use analytics or third-party tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>All traffic is encrypted in transit with HTTPS.</li>
        <li>Passwords are stored as salted one-way hashes, never in readable form.</li>
        <li>Accounts lock automatically after repeated failed sign-in attempts.</li>
        <li>Every section of the system checks your role before showing or changing data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Keeping and removing data</h2>
    <p>
        School records are kept for as long as the school needs them for its registers.
        Staff accounts can be disabled or removed by an administrator at any time. If you
        believe a record about you is incorrect, or you would like it removed, contact
        your school administrator and they can correct or delete it from within STDMS.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a
        new "last updated" date.
    </p>
</div>
